# Valgrind suppression file for QR-UOV (all parameter sets, ref implementation).
# QR-UOV does not claim constant-time signing (see docs/algorithms/sig/qruov.yml,
# no-secret-dependent-branching-claimed: false). These are the secret-dependent
# operations that valgrind reports, recorded so they are tracked rather than
# silenced.

# The pivot search branches on the zero pattern of a matrix derived from the
# secret key, which leaks pivot positions and rank.
{
   Pivot search in the LU decomposition of a secret-derived matrix
   Memcheck:Cond
   src:linsys.c:38
}

# A cache-timing channel, although the table is small (q bytes).
{
   Field inversion by table lookup indexed by a secret-derived pivot
   Memcheck:Value8
   src:gf.h:53
}

# The branch is on the signature vector s, which is published in canonical
# form, but whether it was negated reveals one bit about the value computed
# before canonicalisation. Believed harmless; recorded here rather than in
# passes until that is confirmed.
{
   Canonicalisation of the signature vector s
   Memcheck:Cond
   src:qruov_common.c:22
}

{
   Canonicalisation of the signature vector s
   Memcheck:Cond
   src:qruov_common.c:31
}

{
   Canonicalisation of the signature vector s
   Memcheck:Cond
   src:qruov_common.c:33
}

# TODO: human audit of these is still required to verify CT-claims
# claude-opus-5.5:
#   avx2 implementation only. The rejection sampler compacts accepted
#   coefficients with shuffle masks looked up by the rejection pattern
#   (bextmask[mask], bdepmask[mask]), and its loop bounds and memset lengths
#   depend on how many coefficients were rejected. Some of the sampled buffers
#   are derived from secret seeds, so this leaks the positions and number of
#   rejected samples. The fastop_* helpers are static and also exist in the
#   ref and opt implementations, so each entry is anchored to an avx2 caller.
{
   AVX2 rejection sampling: shuffle-mask lookup indexed by the rejection pattern
   Memcheck:Value8
   ...
   fun:fastop_rejsamp_prep
   ...
   fun:qruov_*_avx2_*
}
{
   AVX2 rejection sampling: loop bounds depend on the number of rejected samples
   Memcheck:Cond
   ...
   fun:fastop_rejsamp_prep
   ...
   fun:qruov_*_avx2_*
}
{
   AVX2 rejection sampling: shuffle-mask lookup indexed by the rejection pattern
   Memcheck:Value8
   ...
   fun:fastop_rejection_sample
   fun:qruov_*_avx2_rejection_sample
}
{
   AVX2 rejection sampling: loop bounds depend on the number of rejected samples
   Memcheck:Cond
   ...
   fun:fastop_rejection_sample
   fun:qruov_*_avx2_rejection_sample
}
